ble snob. She looks            on most other people.\n                     6  | didn’t have time to read the newspaper yesterday. | only looked            it very quickly.\n               9.3.   Complete  the diagram using words from the opposite page.\n\n                the end of the exams                                                   bean\n\n                                            to                                  on, without getting involved\n\n\n                        carefully                                                           for the police\n                               Fa                                           while she steals the bike\n             our plans for the future and\n             make  a decision                                                        act as the\n\n\n               9.4    Here are some more  phrasal verbs based on look. Read each sentence and try to guess the\n                      meaning  of the phrasal verb. Use a dictionary if necessary.\n        Cambridge\n                        You could look up the new words in a dictionary.\n\n        Dictionary\n                        When  | was in Boston on business last week | looked up an old friend.\n                         After a long recession the economic situation is looking up.\n   dictionary.cambridge.org\n                         | looked over the report on the way to the meeting.\n                         | looked through the report and scribbled down a few notes.\n                         Detectives are looking into the murder.\n\n\n                                                                    English Phrasal Verbs in Use Intermediate   23", "char_count": 3613, "mean_conf": 91.34, "word_count": 444, "words": [{"text": "Exercises", "x0": 432, "y0": 101, "x1": 786, "y1": 171, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "9.1", "x0": 288, "y0": 312, "x1": 362, "y1": 353, "conf": 70, "bold": false}, {"text": "Choose", "x0": 433, "y0": 317, "x1": 580, "y1